                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Added a check there based on your example code \ud83d\ude0a"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 117,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we want to do a little code golf here?\n\n```\nif (value.size() == 0){\n   return true;\n}\nnlohmann::json::type first_type = value[0].type();\nstd::ranges::all_of(value, [first_type](const json& el){ return el.type() == first_type; }\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 117,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, we can avoid the loop with ranges algorithm, code becomes shorter but we have an inline lambda now.\nNo complain, it is very short. Adjusted the code as described \ud83d\udc4d"
                }
